It uses only Python integers, Fraction, integer square root, and standard
metadata/JSON facilities. No float enters its enclosure arithmetic.

A complex rectangle is (real_lo,real_hi,imag_lo,imag_hi)/S with S=2^128.
Real products use the extrema of all four integer corner products. Complex
products enclose ac-bd and ad+bc before outward division by S. Division by
positive d uses floor n//d and ceiling -((-n)//d). Exact Gaussian-integer
left multiplication uses signed endpoint order and no rounding. All five
A/E coefficient matrices have an exact common rational denominator; the
recurrence first accumulates the sparse Gaussian-integer numerators, then
divides outward once by denominator*(n+1). Horner evaluation at 1/8 divides
outward at every stage. These operations inductively enclose each exact
coefficient, value and product, without an assumption of independent errors.

Chronological composition within a slot is

    U_new=U_step U_old,
    D_new=D_step U_old+U_step D_old.

The program evaluates D_new before replacing U_old. For global products,
prefix[j]=U_(j-1)...U_0 and suffix[j]=U_23...U_j. Thus

    D_global,j=suffix[j+1] D_slot,j prefix[j].

It constructs -i U_global^dagger D_global,j, using a genuine conjugate
transpose. Pauli traces use Tr(PH)=sum_(i,k)P_(i,k)H_(k,i), not a bilinear
entrywise product. These ordering, adjoint and scalar conditions are all
load-bearing; a successful residual inequality cannot substitute for their
